    <item>
      <title>GitHub &gt; Render</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/</guid>
      <description>&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/sign-in.png&#34;alt=&#34;Render homepage&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Render homepage&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click SIGN IN button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/sign-in-with-github.png&#34;alt=&#34;Sign into Render using GitHub&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Sign into Render using GitHub&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Choose GitHub as your sign in method&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/authorise-render.png&#34;alt=&#34;Authorise Render to access GitHub&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Authorise Render to access GitHub&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click Authorise Render button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/complete-sign-up.png&#34;alt=&#34;Complete sign up with Render&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Complete sign up with Render&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click COMPLETE SIGN UP button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/verification-email-sent.png&#34;alt=&#34;Verification email sent by Render&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Verification email sent by Render&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Head on over to your mailbox&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/verification-email-received.png&#34;alt=&#34;Verification email received in mailbox&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Verification email received in mailbox&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Check your inbox for Activation request&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Deploy a server</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/deploying-server/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/deploying-server/</guid>
      <description>&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Make sure you have connected your GitHub account to Render (see &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-github/&#34;&gt;How to connect your GitHub to Render&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/deploying-server/render-dashboard.png&#34;alt=&#34;Render dashboard&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Render dashboard&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Log into the Render dashboard&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/deploying-server/dashboard-new-button.png&#34;alt=&#34;New &amp;#43; button on dashboard&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;New &amp;#43; button on dashboard&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click on the New + button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/deploying-server/new-web-service.jpg&#34;alt=&#34;Select Web Service from the New &amp;#43; button dropdown&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Select Web Service from the New &amp;#43; button dropdown&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click on Web Service from the dropdown list&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/deploying-server/connect-repo.jpg&#34;alt=&#34;Connect repo to Render&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Connect repo to Render&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Select your repo to connect to Render by clicking on the Connect button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>PostgreSQL &gt; Render</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/creating-a-postgres-db/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/creating-a-postgres-db/</guid>
      <description>&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/creating-a-postgres-db/new-postgres.png&#34;alt=&#34;Click on PostgreSQL in the New &amp;#43; dropdown&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Click on PostgreSQL in the New &amp;#43; dropdown&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Click on the &lt;strong&gt;New +&lt;/strong&gt; button, then click on PostgreSQL&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Fill out the Name field, which will be used to label the database within Render. Fill out the Database and User fields, which should be the same as your development environment - ask a volunteer if you are unsure. Leave the remaining 3 input fields as is with the default values &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/creating-a-postgres-db/database-name.png&#34;alt=&#34;Provide a Name, Database and User&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Provide a Name, Database and User&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Provide a Name, Database and User&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>client &gt; database</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-a-dbms/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-a-dbms/</guid>
      <description>&lt;section class=&#34;c-note c-note--tip&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;h4 class=&#34;c-note__title e-heading__4&#34;&gt;💡Tip&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/h4&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;c-note__text &#34;&gt;This guide uses a database client called &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://dbeaver.io/&#34;&gt;DBeaver&lt;/a&gt;, but the ideas still apply if you are using another client. If you are using another client, try looking for similarly named controls.&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-a-dbms/new-connection.png&#34;alt=&#34;Creating a new Database Connection&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Creating a new Database Connection&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Navigate to the Database tab and select New Database Connection&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-a-dbms/selecting-postgres.png&#34;alt=&#34;Selecting PostgreSQL from the available databases&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Selecting PostgreSQL from the available databases&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Select PostgreSQL then click the Next button&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Often, after the first installation or use of a specific database type, you may encounter the download of relevant drivers modal. This is perfectly normal, just click Download and proceed to the next step. DBeaver will download and install the relevant drivers needed for using your specific database type &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;      &lt;img&#xD;&#xA;        loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xD;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/connecting-a-dbms/db-drivers.png&#34;alt=&#34;Downloading PostgreSQL drivers&#34; data-pagefind-index-attrs=&#34;Downloading PostgreSQL drivers&#34;/&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;click Download and proceed to the next step&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Serving frontend through backend</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/serving-frontend-through-backend/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/render/serving-frontend-through-backend/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Render support frontend deployments either via their CDN, or by changing your backend code to support serving frontend files. If you wish CDN style deployment we suggest you use Netlify instead. For a guide on how to update your backend to support serving frontend files please read &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/deploying/flyio/serving-frontend/&#34;&gt;the Fly.io frontend guide&lt;/a&gt; guide.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
